From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Zach Taylor <zctaylor.work@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 17:57:53 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 30/30] Register the isolated native worker from verified Pod
 identity

The isolated Fabriek candidate plane runs one Deployment with no
WorkerPool and no worker-pool label, so shared worker discovery never
registers it. kubectl ate admin register-static-worker observes the exact
Pod (UID, node, placement, image digest, Ready state, container identity),
requires the private API binding, and creates or replays that one worker.
It is registered UNAVAILABLE with the SPIFFE ID of the Pod service account;
the worker process reports its own capacity, IPs and runtimes.

The command never updates or deletes a registration, refuses an unexpected
inventory, and re-observes the Pod after the create. Image identity comes
from the runtime ImageID manifest reference, because some runtimes show a
configuration digest as the displayed image.

Fork-Topic: static-worker
Fork-Upstream: fork-only
